From 7269bacada069abcb8f57a27e0c2dca4af4816c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Correct beat route in the content contract
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The spec said /news/<beat>, which collides with /news/<slug> — a post
slugged "humanoids" would be ambiguous with the humanoids beat page.
The implementation already uses /topics/<beat>; this brings the document
in line and records why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoP27rzu54WHAfQwNd6sTn
---
 docs/content-contract-v2.md | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/content-contract-v2.md b/docs/content-contract-v2.md
index 96e2b0a..1206167 100644
--- a/docs/content-contract-v2.md
+++ b/docs/content-contract-v2.md
@@ -255,7 +255,9 @@ Derived automatically from frontmatter. The automation does not produce these, b
 are only correct if the frontmatter is:
 
 - `/news` — index, newest first by `publishedAt`, paginated
-- `/news/<beat>` — a landing page per beat in §4
+- `/topics/<beat>` — a landing page per beat in §4. **Corrected from `/news/<beat>`**,
+  which collided with `/news/<slug>`: a post slugged `humanoids` would have been
+  ambiguous with the humanoids beat page. `/topics/` removes the class of bug.
 - `/rss.xml` — full feed
 - `NewsArticle` JSON-LD per post, using `title`, `description`, `publishedAt`,
   `updatedAt`, `author.name` and `image.light`
-- 
